§ `Section 18(h): periods of time`

-- "from" a day includes that day; the last day of a period of N days is the Nth day counting the first as day 1.
-- A period "after" an event is not governed by the text: it refuses.
-- Weeks, calendar months and years are counted only from the day on which the defined unit itself begins (a Sunday, the first of a month, 1 January):
-- beginning anywhere else the text gives no rule, and the module refuses; see NOTES.md, forks F4 to F6, for the readings it did not take.

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`n is a whole number of at least one` n MEANS
    n AT LEAST 1 AND FLOOR n EQUALS n

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` n `days beginning on or reckoned from` d MEANS
    IF   `n is a whole number of at least one` n
    THEN d PLUS (n MINUS 1)
    ELSE `a period must be a whole number of units, at least one`

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
-- src:245 | “week” means the period between midnight on any Saturday and midnight on the following Saturday;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h); Schedule Pt 1 "week" (src:177, src:245)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` n `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` d MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `n is a whole number of at least one` n THEN `a period must be a whole number of units, at least one`
           IF NOT `is the first day of a week` d          THEN `the Act has no rule for a period of weeks that does not begin on a Sunday`
           OTHERWISE d PLUS ((7 TIMES n) MINUS 1)

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
-- src:232 | “month” means a calendar month;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h); Schedule Pt 1 "month" (src:177, src:232)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` n `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` d MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `n is a whole number of at least one` n THEN `a period must be a whole number of units, at least one`
           IF DATE_DAY d GREATER THAN 1                    THEN `the Act has no rule for a period of calendar months that does not begin on the first day of a month`
           OTHERWISE (`the calendar month containing` (`add months` d (n MINUS 1)))'s `its last day`

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
-- src:248 | “year”, when used without qualification, means a period of 12 months beginning on the 1st day of January in any year.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h); Schedule Pt 1 "year" (src:177, src:248)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` n `years beginning on or reckoned from` d MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `n is a whole number of at least one` n THEN `a period must be a whole number of units, at least one`
           IF NOT (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 1) THEN `the Act has no rule for a period of years that does not begin on 1 January`
           OTHERWISE YMD (DATE_YEAR d PLUS (n MINUS 1)) 12 31

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177)
GIVEN p IS A `A period of time`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the period` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `how it is counted`
    WHEN `from a day` THEN
        CONSIDER p's `its unit`
        WHEN Days              THEN `the last day of a period of` (p's `its length`) `days beginning on or reckoned from` (p's `the day it is counted from`)
        WHEN Weeks             THEN `the last day of a period of` (p's `its length`) `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` (p's `the day it is counted from`)
        WHEN `Calendar months` THEN `the last day of a period of` (p's `its length`) `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (p's `the day it is counted from`)
        WHEN Years             THEN `the last day of a period of` (p's `its length`) `years beginning on or reckoned from` (p's `the day it is counted from`)
    WHEN `after an event` THEN `section 18(h) says nothing about a period counted after an event`

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177)
GIVEN p IS A `A period of time`
GIVETH A Span
`the span of the period` p MEANS
    Span WITH `its first day` IS p's `the day it is counted from`
              `its last day`  IS `the last day of the period` p

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      f IS A DATE
      l IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day` d `falls within the period beginning on` f `and ending on` l MEANS
    d AT LEAST f AND d AT MOST l

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      p IS A `A period of time`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day` d `falls within the period` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `how it is counted`
    WHEN `from a day`    THEN d AT LEAST start AND (d EQUALS start OR d AT MOST `the last day of the period` p)
    WHEN `after an event` THEN IF   d LESS THAN start
                               THEN FALSE
                               ELSE `section 18(h) says nothing about a period counted after an event`
    WHERE
        start MEANS p's `the day it is counted from`

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177)
GIVEN f IS A DATE
      l IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in the period beginning on` f `and ending on` l MEANS
    (Day l MINUS Day f) PLUS 1

§ `Days of rest, recess and holiday`

-- The Act contains no provision that moves the last day of a period off a day of rest, recess or holiday.
-- So the last day is returned when it is not such a day, and the module refuses when it is, whatever follows it.
-- Which days are days of rest, recess or holiday under some other enactment is an INPUT.

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177); no provision of the text moves a last day
GIVEN `the last day` IS A DATE
      `rest days`    IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` `the last day` `rest days` MEANS
    IF   `rest days` `the last day`
    THEN `the Act has no rule for a last day that falls on a day of rest, recess or holiday; another enactment or rules of court may have one`
    ELSE `the last day`

§ `The Schedule, Parts 1 and 2: the Act's time words`

-- src:230 | “midnight” means, in relation to a particular day, the point of time at which the day ends;
-- src:245 | “week” means the period between midnight on any Saturday and midnight on the following Saturday;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "week" (src:245); "midnight" (src:230)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A Span
`the week containing` d MEANS
    Span WITH `its first day` IS d MINUS `Weekday of` d
              `its last day`  IS (d MINUS `Weekday of` d) PLUS 6

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is the first day of a week` d MEANS
    `Weekday of` d EQUALS 0

-- src:232 | “month” means a calendar month;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "month" (src:232)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A Span
`the calendar month containing` d MEANS
    Span WITH `its first day` IS YMD (DATE_YEAR d) (DATE_MONTH d) 1
              `its last day`  IS YMD (DATE_YEAR d) (DATE_MONTH d) (`Days in month` (DATE_MONTH d) (DATE_YEAR d))

-- src:248 | “year”, when used without qualification, means a period of 12 months beginning on the 1st day of January in any year.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "year" (src:248)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A Span
`the year containing` d MEANS
    Span WITH `its first day` IS YMD (DATE_YEAR d) 1 1
              `its last day`  IS YMD (DATE_YEAR d) 12 31

-- src:224 | “financial year”, in relation to an exchequer financial year, means the period which is coextensive with a calendar year;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "financial year" (src:224)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A Span
`the exchequer financial year containing` d MEANS
    `the year containing` d

-- src:229 | “local financial year” means a period which is coextensive with a calendar year;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "local financial year" (src:229)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A Span
`the local financial year containing` d MEANS
    `the year containing` d

-- src:246 | “week-day” means a day which is not a Sunday;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "week-day" (src:246)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a week-day` d MEANS
    `Weekday of` d GREATER THAN 0

-- src:255 | “public holiday” means a public holiday determined in accordance with the Organisation of Working Time Act 1997 ;
-- src:257 | “working day” means a day which is not a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "working day" (src:257); "public holiday" (src:255)
GIVEN d              IS A DATE
      `public holidays` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a working day` d `public holidays` MEANS
        `is weekday` d
    AND NOT `public holidays` d

GIVEN remaining         IS A NUMBER
      d                 IS A DATE
      `public holidays` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
      fuel              IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day on which the remaining working days are completed` remaining d `public holidays` fuel MEANS
    BRANCH IF fuel AT MOST 0 THEN `no day was found within the search limit`
           IF `is a working day` d `public holidays`
              THEN (IF   remaining EQUALS 1
                    THEN d
                    ELSE `the day on which the remaining working days are completed` (remaining MINUS 1) (d PLUS 1) `public holidays` (fuel MINUS 1))
           OTHERWISE `the day on which the remaining working days are completed` remaining (d PLUS 1) `public holidays` (fuel MINUS 1)

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
-- src:257 | “working day” means a day which is not a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h); Schedule Pt 2 "working day" (src:177, src:257)
GIVEN n                 IS A NUMBER
      d                 IS A DATE
      `public holidays` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` n `working days beginning on or reckoned from` d `, public holidays being` `public holidays` MEANS
    IF   `n is a whole number of at least one` n
    THEN `the day on which the remaining working days are completed` n d `public holidays` 4000
    ELSE `a period must be a whole number of units, at least one`

GIVEN remaining IS A NUMBER
      d         IS A DATE
      fuel      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day on which the remaining week-days are completed` remaining d fuel MEANS
    BRANCH IF fuel AT MOST 0 THEN `no day was found within the search limit`
           IF `is a week-day` d
              THEN (IF   remaining EQUALS 1
                    THEN d
                    ELSE `the day on which the remaining week-days are completed` (remaining MINUS 1) (d PLUS 1) (fuel MINUS 1))
           OTHERWISE `the day on which the remaining week-days are completed` remaining (d PLUS 1) (fuel MINUS 1)

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
-- src:246 | “week-day” means a day which is not a Sunday;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h); Schedule Pt 1 "week-day" (src:177, src:246)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` n `week-days beginning on or reckoned from` d MEANS
