    THEN `the day on which the remaining week-days are completed` n d 4000
    ELSE `a period must be a whole number of units, at least one`

§ `Section 18(i): a time expressed by reference to an hour`

-- src:178 | (i) Time. Where time is expressed by reference to a specified hour or to a time before or after a specified hour, that time shall be determined by reference to the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971 ;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(i) (src:178)
GIVEN hour IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the clock time of a specified hour in an enactment` hour MEANS
    `the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971 is not in the text of this Act and is not encoded`

§ `Sections 15 and 16: the day, and the moment, from which an enactment is in operation`

-- "binds" is not a word the Act uses; the Act says "comes into operation", and the Schedule says that "commencement" is "the time at which the enactment comes into operation".

-- src:153 | Date of passing of Acts of Oireachtas. 15.—(1) The date of the passing of an Act of the Oireachtas is the date of the day on which the Bill for the Act is signed by the President.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 15(1) (src:153)
GIVEN `the day the Bill was signed by the President` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date of the passing of an Act of the Oireachtas signed on` `the day the Bill was signed by the President` MEANS
    `the day the Bill was signed by the President`

-- src:155 | Commencement. 16.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), every provision of an Act comes into operation on the date of its passing.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16(1) (src:155)
GIVEN passed IS A DATE
GIVETH A Commencement
`section 16(1) commencement` passed MEANS
    Commencement WITH `the day the text names`     IS passed
                      `the moment the text fixes`  IS NOTHING
                      `the provision that decides` IS "section 16(1)"

-- src:156 | (2) Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the passing of the Act and whether the day is named in the Act or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the Act or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16(2) (src:156)
GIVEN particular IS A DATE
GIVETH A Commencement
`section 16(2) commencement` particular MEANS
    Commencement WITH `the day the text names`     IS particular
                      `the moment the text fixes`  IS JUST (Midnight WITH `the day it ends` IS particular MINUS 1)
                      `the provision that decides` IS "section 16(2)"

-- src:157 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), every provision of a statutory instrument comes into operation at the end of the day before the day on which the statutory instrument is made.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16(3) (src:157)
GIVEN made IS A DATE
GIVETH A Commencement
`section 16(3) commencement` made MEANS
    Commencement WITH `the day the text names`     IS made
                      `the moment the text fixes`  IS JUST (Midnight WITH `the day it ends` IS made MINUS 1)
                      `the provision that decides` IS "section 16(3)"

-- src:158 | (4) Where a statutory instrument or a provision of a statutory instrument is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the making of the statutory instrument and whether the day is named in the instrument or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the statutory instrument or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16(4) (src:158)
GIVEN particular IS A DATE
GIVETH A Commencement
`section 16(4) commencement` particular MEANS
    Commencement WITH `the day the text names`     IS particular
                      `the moment the text fixes`  IS JUST (Midnight WITH `the day it ends` IS particular MINUS 1)
                      `the provision that decides` IS "section 16(4)"

-- src:155 | Commencement. 16.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), every provision of an Act comes into operation on the date of its passing.
-- src:156 | (2) Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the passing of the Act and whether the day is named in the Act or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the Act or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16(1), (2) (src:155-156)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
GIVETH A Commencement
`the commencement of an Act` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `what it says about commencement`
    WHEN `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` THEN
        CONSIDER facts's `the day of its passing or making`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day of the passing or the making was not supplied`
        WHEN JUST passed THEN `section 16(1) commencement` passed
    WHEN `it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` particular THEN `section 16(2) commencement` particular
    WHEN `it is expressed to come into operation on a day not yet fixed or ascertained` THEN `the particular day on which the enactment is to come into operation has not been fixed or ascertained`

-- src:153 | Date of passing of Acts of Oireachtas. 15.—(1) The date of the passing of an Act of the Oireachtas is the date of the day on which the Bill for the Act is signed by the President.
-- src:155 | Commencement. 16.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), every provision of an Act comes into operation on the date of its passing.
-- src:156 | (2) Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the passing of the Act and whether the day is named in the Act or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the Act or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 ss 15(1), 16(1), (2) (src:153, src:155-156)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
GIVETH A Commencement
`the commencement of a Saorstat Eireann statute` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `what it says about commencement`
    WHEN `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` THEN `section 15(1) defines the date of passing only for an Act of the Oireachtas`
    WHEN `it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` particular THEN `section 16(2) commencement` particular
    WHEN `it is expressed to come into operation on a day not yet fixed or ascertained` THEN `the particular day on which the enactment is to come into operation has not been fixed or ascertained`

-- src:157 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), every provision of a statutory instrument comes into operation at the end of the day before the day on which the statutory instrument is made.
-- src:158 | (4) Where a statutory instrument or a provision of a statutory instrument is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the making of the statutory instrument and whether the day is named in the instrument or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the statutory instrument or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16(3), (4) (src:157-158)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
GIVETH A Commencement
`the commencement of a statutory instrument` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `what it says about commencement`
    WHEN `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` THEN
        CONSIDER facts's `the day of its passing or making`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day of the passing or the making was not supplied`
        WHEN JUST made THEN `section 16(3) commencement` made
    WHEN `it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` particular THEN `section 16(4) commencement` particular
    WHEN `it is expressed to come into operation on a day not yet fixed or ascertained` THEN `the particular day on which the enactment is to come into operation has not been fixed or ascertained`

-- src:155 | Commencement. 16.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), every provision of an Act comes into operation on the date of its passing.
-- src:156 | (2) Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the passing of the Act and whether the day is named in the Act or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the Act or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
-- src:157 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), every provision of a statutory instrument comes into operation at the end of the day before the day on which the statutory instrument is made.
-- src:158 | (4) Where a statutory instrument or a provision of a statutory instrument is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the making of the statutory instrument and whether the day is named in the instrument or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the statutory instrument or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16 (src:155-158)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
GIVETH A Commencement
`the commencement of` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `its kind`
    WHEN `an Act of the Oireachtas`                                     THEN `the commencement of an Act` facts
    WHEN `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force`             THEN `the commencement of a Saorstat Eireann statute` facts
    WHEN `a statutory instrument`                                       THEN `the commencement of a statutory instrument` facts

-- src:155 | Commencement. 16.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), every provision of an Act comes into operation on the date of its passing.
-- src:156 | (2) Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the passing of the Act and whether the day is named in the Act or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the Act or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
-- src:157 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), every provision of a statutory instrument comes into operation at the end of the day before the day on which the statutory instrument is made.
-- src:158 | (4) Where a statutory instrument or a provision of a statutory instrument is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the making of the statutory instrument and whether the day is named in the instrument or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the statutory instrument or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16(1)-(4) (src:155-158)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day on which the enactment comes into operation, as the text names it` facts MEANS
    (`the commencement of` facts)'s `the day the text names`

-- src:155 | Commencement. 16.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), every provision of an Act comes into operation on the date of its passing.
-- src:156 | (2) Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the passing of the Act and whether the day is named in the Act or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the Act or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
-- src:157 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), every provision of a statutory instrument comes into operation at the end of the day before the day on which the statutory instrument is made.
-- src:158 | (4) Where a statutory instrument or a provision of a statutory instrument is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the making of the statutory instrument and whether the day is named in the instrument or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the statutory instrument or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16(2)-(4) (src:156-158); s 16(1) names none (src:155)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
GIVETH A Midnight
`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER (`the commencement of` facts)'s `the moment the text fixes`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `section 16(1) names no moment within the date of passing`
    WHEN JUST m THEN m

-- src:220 | “commencement”, when used in relation to an enactment, means the time at which the enactment comes into operation;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "commencement" (src:220)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
GIVETH A Midnight
`the commencement of the enactment, as the Schedule defines the word` facts MEANS
    `the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` facts

-- src:155 | Commencement. 16.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), every provision of an Act comes into operation on the date of its passing.
-- src:156 | (2) Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the passing of the Act and whether the day is named in the Act or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the Act or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
-- src:157 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), every provision of a statutory instrument comes into operation at the end of the day before the day on which the statutory instrument is made.
-- src:158 | (4) Where a statutory instrument or a provision of a statutory instrument is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the making of the statutory instrument and whether the day is named in the instrument or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the statutory instrument or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
-- src:230 | “midnight” means, in relation to a particular day, the point of time at which the day ends;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16(1)-(4) (src:155-158); Schedule Pt 1 "midnight" (src:230)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
      d     IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the enactment` facts `is in operation at the end of` d MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the moment the text fixes`
    WHEN JUST m   THEN d AT LEAST m's `the day it ends`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN d AT LEAST c's `the day the text names`
    WHERE
        c MEANS `the commencement of` facts

-- src:155 | Commencement. 16.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), every provision of an Act comes into operation on the date of its passing.
-- src:156 | (2) Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the passing of the Act and whether the day is named in the Act or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the Act or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
-- src:157 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), every provision of a statutory instrument comes into operation at the end of the day before the day on which the statutory instrument is made.
-- src:158 | (4) Where a statutory instrument or a provision of a statutory instrument is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the making of the statutory instrument and whether the day is named in the instrument or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the statutory instrument or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
-- src:230 | “midnight” means, in relation to a particular day, the point of time at which the day ends;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16(1)-(4) (src:155-158); Schedule Pt 1 "midnight" (src:230)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
      d     IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the enactment` facts `is in operation throughout` d MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the moment the text fixes`
    WHEN JUST m   THEN d AT LEAST (m's `the day it ends` PLUS 1)
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN BRANCH IF d GREATER THAN c's `the day the text names` THEN TRUE
                              IF d LESS THAN c's `the day the text names`    THEN FALSE
                              OTHERWISE `the moment within a day at which the enactment comes into operation is not fixed by the text, so whether the whole of that day is in operation is not answered`
    WHERE
        c MEANS `the commencement of` facts

-- src:155 | Commencement. 16.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), every provision of an Act comes into operation on the date of its passing.
-- src:156 | (2) Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the passing of the Act and whether the day is named in the Act or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the Act or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
-- src:157 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), every provision of a statutory instrument comes into operation at the end of the day before the day on which the statutory instrument is made.
-- src:158 | (4) Where a statutory instrument or a provision of a statutory instrument is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the making of the statutory instrument and whether the day is named in the instrument or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the statutory instrument or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
-- src:230 | “midnight” means, in relation to a particular day, the point of time at which the day ends;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16(1)-(4) (src:155-158); Schedule Pt 1 "midnight" (src:230)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day on which the enactment is in operation throughout` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the moment the text fixes`
    WHEN JUST m   THEN m's `the day it ends` PLUS 1
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN `the moment within a day at which the enactment comes into operation is not fixed by the text, so whether the whole of that day is in operation is not answered`
    WHERE
        c MEANS `the commencement of` facts

-- src:157 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), every provision of a statutory instrument comes into operation at the end of the day before the day on which the statutory instrument is made.
-- src:158 | (4) Where a statutory instrument or a provision of a statutory instrument is expressed to come into operation on a particular day (whether the day is before or after the date of the making of the statutory instrument and whether the day is named in the instrument or is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner), the statutory instrument or provision comes into operation at the end of the day before the particular day.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 16(3), (4) (src:157-158)
GIVEN `what it says`   IS A `What an enactment says about its own commencement`
      `the day it was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day on which a statutory instrument is in operation throughout` `what it says` `the day it was made` MEANS
    `the first day on which the enactment is in operation throughout` facts
    WHERE
        facts MEANS `Facts about an enactment` WITH
            `its kind`                         IS `a statutory instrument`
            `what it says about commencement`  IS `what it says`
            `the day of its passing or making` IS JUST `the day it was made`

§ `Section 1(2): the commencement of this Act`

-- src:80 | [17th October, 2005]
-- src:84 | (2) This Act comes into operation on 1 January 2006.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 1(2) (src:84); the date of its passing, endorsed under s 15(2) (src:80)
`the facts about this Act` MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment` WITH
        `its kind`                         IS `an Act of the Oireachtas`
